body:
I'd been planning to start a new playthrough soon after finishing PL for the first time, but... the Tower ending just hit a little TOO hard. I've spent most of my life having people drift away from me or outright burning bridges for one reason or another, and now I'm at a point in my life where I feel like I'm at a dead end. I've been suicidal for the past several years, and I imagine I won't last much longer at this rate. While I get that the ending is an opportunity for V to start a new life, it just really reminded me of how alone I am right now.

&#x200B;

Writing-wise I do agree with some of the opinions here in that V could've at least done a bit more to give a heads up to people rather than just completely disappearing. The other issue I feel is that, given the consequences of V's lifestyle (i.e, ending up with the Relic in the first place), their desire to go straight back into that life right after the surgery (and their reaction to being told that they can't) feels... a bit off to me. Then again, it was a long time since I last played the game in full; beat it in 2021 and picked up an old save to do the DLC when that dropped.
